                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d42c38b4-95f0-3fa9-b214-ab23d3735f08",
                        "entry_id": "20ed0dc0-b9d1-3c5d-a03a-255278af6432",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Röntgenstrahl oder (übertragen) Röntgenstrahlung"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic",
                            "plural-normally"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c1e90582-5b01-4029-b6e7-5742110916f0",
                                "sense_id": "d42c38b4-95f0-3fa9-b214-ab23d3735f08",
                                "text": "„Vom X-Strahl zum Atommodell […] Die X-Strahlen – so nannte sie ihr Entdecker – waren nämlich magnetisch nicht ablenkbar und besaßen auch ein beträchtlich stärkeres Durchdringungsvermögen als die Kathodenstrahlen[.]“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "796c053a-b109-4d94-a473-037069ddafc4",
                                "sense_id": "d42c38b4-95f0-3fa9-b214-ab23d3735f08",
                                "text": "„…; wir sehen ja, dass an spongiösen Knochenteilen, die feinen zum X-Strahl perpendikulär liegenden Lamellen von jenem durchdrungen werden, …“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3dc766a7-01ff-479a-8599-32021d3f767c",
                                "sense_id": "d42c38b4-95f0-3fa9-b214-ab23d3735f08",
                                "text": "„Diese geben einen heilenden X-Strahl im Gegensatz zu der X-Strahlenqualität, die am besten angewandt werden, um ein gutes Skiagraph zu geben.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a410bb3d-82f0-4b1e-80c2-8cdedc37aea3",
                                "sense_id": "d42c38b4-95f0-3fa9-b214-ab23d3735f08",
                                "text": "„Unschädlicher als Sonde und Kugelzange dient der X-Strahl zur exakten Lokalisirung des Geschosses.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "514cd62d-905a-4ebb-ad2a-e027a23e7409",
                                "sense_id": "d42c38b4-95f0-3fa9-b214-ab23d3735f08",
                                "text": "„Die Röntgenstrahlen sind in der Tat polarisiert und zwar so, daſs ihre gröſste Wirkung in der Ebene erfolgt, welche durch den in der Röhre verlaufenden Kathodenstrahl und den durch ihn erzeugten X-Strahl bestimmt ist.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "aff9cd48-0c3e-421c-b338-694b0859e674",
                                "sense_id": "d42c38b4-95f0-3fa9-b214-ab23d3735f08",
                                "text": "„…; denn jeder X-Strahl entsteht ja aus einem Kathodenstrahl und daher ist durch den Kathoden- und X-Strahl eine Ebene fest bestimmt, in der möglicher Weise das Verhalten des X-Strahls ein anderes ist, als in allen anderen Ebenen.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e3455f8e-8c78-4f1d-803c-c3dbbdff4b73",
                        "source_entry_id": "20ed0dc0-b9d1-3c5d-a03a-255278af6432",
                        "source_sense_id": "d42c38b4-95f0-3fa9-b214-ab23d3735f08",
                        "source_sense_description": "veraltet, meist Plural: Röntgenstrahl oder (übertragen) Röntgenstrahlung",
                        "target_lang_word": "X-ray",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "X-ray",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1b296b28-7cd9-3578-8a69-688aa0a4d18a",
                                        "entry_id": "a8b86c0c-7c97-3a8c-9096-6384aca65eab",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Short wavelength electromagnetic radiation usually produced by bombarding a metal target in a vacuum. Used to create images of the internal structure of objects; this is possible because X-rays pass through most objects and can expose photographic film."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bc71d7d2-c0a5-45b5-9cbd-cd6180b52ac1",
                                                "sense_id": "1b296b28-7cd9-3578-8a69-688aa0a4d18a",
                                                "text": "X-rays are light with a wavelength between 0.1 and 10 nm."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2f662f9e-fded-3bf5-95b2-6aa8289828a8",
                                        "entry_id": "a8b86c0c-7c97-3a8c-9096-6384aca65eab",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A radiograph: a photograph made with X-rays."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "81fd8457-507d-4162-a31d-45e5a97ec310",
                                                "sense_id": "2f662f9e-fded-3bf5-95b2-6aa8289828a8",
                                                "text": "The doctor ordered some X-rays of my injured wrist."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "59e7c72d-b98f-439d-bf0d-73f984aab188",
                                                "sense_id": "2f662f9e-fded-3bf5-95b2-6aa8289828a8",
                                                "text": "And this friendly was not without its injury worries, with defender Gary Cahill substituted early on after a nasty, needless push by Dries Mertens that caused him to collide with goalkeeper Joe Hart, an incident that left the Chelsea defender requiring a precautionary X-ray at Wembley."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "921ee723-83b1-329c-9801-77af9b4972f1",
                                        "entry_id": "a8b86c0c-7c97-3a8c-9096-6384aca65eab",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An X-ray machine."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8483fe02-c4f0-31a5-b5f1-fefd94aab18b",
                                        "entry_id": "a8b86c0c-7c97-3a8c-9096-6384aca65eab",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A tactical motif where a piece exerts influence or control over a square, piece, or line indirectly through another intervening piece."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "X-ray",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c1b3a0bf-7b67-3087-898f-10ec1b3bfc72",
                                        "entry_id": "4a40ea0e-ce0b-3476-b50d-5c41c8e48c70",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To take a radiograph of; to obtain an image of using X-ray radiation, especially for the purpose of medical diagnostic evaluation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b0f280e9-306b-4e26-8d11-837b222f09d1",
                                                "sense_id": "c1b3a0bf-7b67-3087-898f-10ec1b3bfc72",
                                                "text": "Of course there was nothing wrong with my left wrist. They X-rayed the wrong arm!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "98f727c1-ccff-4fcc-a0d7-26f8b8dd4755",
                                                "sense_id": "c1b3a0bf-7b67-3087-898f-10ec1b3bfc72",
                                                "text": "1925, Sidney Coe Howard, They Knew What They Wanted (Doubleday, Page and Company), Act II, page 116.\nBoth legs broken in the morning. Tibia, fibula, femur, and ischium. X-rayed and set inside of an hour after the accident."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0a1b847d-0783-3ea3-a1f5-78ba9a7fb8b8",
                                        "entry_id": "4a40ea0e-ce0b-3476-b50d-5c41c8e48c70",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of a piece, to exert indirect influence, by either attacking, defending, or controlling an opponent's or friendly piece through an intervening piece along a rank, file, or diagonal."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "X-ray",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d2479833-5a95-3ccc-8aff-7f64aadc7005",
                                        "entry_id": "008607c6-12ac-34f6-b37a-18fa42f5ae2e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or relating to X-rays."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3b3479cb-1e5d-4587-8e80-28d3a869f648",
                                                "sense_id": "d2479833-5a95-3ccc-8aff-7f64aadc7005",
                                                "text": "I had to put my bags through an X-ray scanner at the airport."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "192b17f1-037e-4043-8bdd-fe539f6b1976",
                                                "sense_id": "d2479833-5a95-3ccc-8aff-7f64aadc7005",
                                                "text": "Who will fly and have X-ray eyes— And be known as the man no bullet can kill?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "96a44d72-ab66-4eff-994a-9a90eb2e4ce7",
                        "source_entry_id": "20ed0dc0-b9d1-3c5d-a03a-255278af6432",
                        "source_sense_id": "d42c38b4-95f0-3fa9-b214-ab23d3735f08",
                        "source_sense_description": "veraltet, meist Plural: Röntgenstrahl oder (übertragen) Röntgenstrahlung",
                        "target_lang_word": "rayon X",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "rayon X",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2f58c024-a103-30a1-aa94-e21e2dcfceaa",
                                        "entry_id": "bde2fef4-1c5f-3701-9aef-07d39eb0a975",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Rayonnement électromagnétique à haute fréquence dont la longueur d’onde est comprise entre 5 picomètres et 10 nanomètres, utilisé pour sa grande capacité à traverser la matière et les tissus sans dommage utilisé en imagerie médicale et dans les portiques de sécurité ; il est aussi largement utilisé en cristallographie afin d’en décrire la structure des matériaux traversés et en astrophysique pour l’exploration spatiale."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "physical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a42cc694-a74f-4d9a-ad0e-0ea28d1ed073",
                                                "sense_id": "2f58c024-a103-30a1-aa94-e21e2dcfceaa",
                                                "text": "En raison de la nature du rayonnement, inconnu à l’époque, le savant le qualifie de « rayon X »."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2d2c5c3a-4a25-49b8-a6d8-b22c3c306fdd",
                                                "sense_id": "2f58c024-a103-30a1-aa94-e21e2dcfceaa",
                                                "text": "Entre mars et mai 1896, Henri Becquerel réalise des expériences au Muséum national d’histoire naturelle afin de déterminer si l’exposition à la lumière de certains sels produisait une émission de rayons X que venait de découvrir Wilhelm Röntgen."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e1489dac-37b6-4290-ae0d-96bd001714e1",
                                                "sense_id": "2f58c024-a103-30a1-aa94-e21e2dcfceaa",
                                                "text": "Les rayons X par transmission (XRT) fonctionnent selon le principe de la radioscopie. Ils permettent la détection des métaux, la qualité du tri étant d’autant meilleure que les métaux présentent des masses atomiques éloignées."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "22451da4-3cdb-4f4d-96b5-a4384b657431",
                                                "sense_id": "2f58c024-a103-30a1-aa94-e21e2dcfceaa",
                                                "text": "Lorsque, le 2 février 1903, M. Blondlot, professeur de physique à la Faculté des Sciences de l’Université de Nancy, membre correspondant de l’Académie des Sciences, adressait à cette académie une note sur la polarisation des rayons X, considérés jusque-là comme impolarisables, qui donc eût pu prévoir que cette petite question de physique pure allait soulever des problèmes passionnants et des controverses […]."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b121ab86-c117-46d3-9b9d-2a68d45acf96",
                        "source_entry_id": "20ed0dc0-b9d1-3c5d-a03a-255278af6432",
